ARM: OMAP2: n8x0-maemo: sink for BME's STI trace records

BME sends a trace record over NETLINK_USERSOCK for each of its events,
to the kernel's STI (OMAP serial trace port) interface of Nokia's
kernel (sti-netlink.c). With no kernel socket for the protocol every
send failed with ECONNREFUSED, and BME printed "sendmsg: Connection
refused" to the console dozens of times a minute (strace on the device:
nlmsg_type 0xc101, STI_WRITE with id 0xc1, channel 0x2b, 32 bytes).
There is no STI: take the records and drop them, ack on request.

--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/n8x0-maemo.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/n8x0-maemo.c
@@ -16,6 +16,8 @@
